35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The data is clear. Projects succeed when access is shared. Older blocks are traps, adding months of delay.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,"The timetable shows we paid for off-site space for two terms. Meanwhile, specialist rooms sit idle, yet general requests are rejected.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"The freeze left posts empty, yet technicians still perform manual checks weekly. We are wasting labor on tasks machines should handle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The data confirms my fear. Comfort-driven projects slip a year, while inspection fixes stay on schedule. We must prioritize compliance over appeal.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The reserve is empty. We bought expensive gear, wrote it off, and forgot to fund its replacement. That’s a silent tax on future budgets.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, compliance is necessary, but not sufficient. My data shows shared access drives satisfaction. We must avoid single-wing projects.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, shared access is vital, but my data shows the real cost is displaced students. We must stop paying for off-site space.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
